const GRAMMAR={
1:{title:'Future forms',what:'Three ways to talk about future events.',why:'Show whether an event is a timetable, an arrangement, or an intention/prediction.',source:'Unit 1 Extra Activities p.2 + Extra Activities Key 1.2; Interactive Homework 1 p.2',body:()=>`
${ar('لا تختَر الزمن لأن الجملة تحتوي على tomorrow أو ساعة محددة فقط. اسأل: هل أصف جدولًا ثابتًا، أم ترتيبًا مع أشخاص، أم نية أو تنبؤًا له دليل؟')}
${table(['Form','Structure','Use + original example'],[
['Present Simple','I/you/we/they + base verb<br>he/she/it + verb-s','Timetables / scheduled events<br><strong>The training session starts at eight.</strong>'],
['Present Continuous','am / is / are + verb-ing','Future arrangements<br><strong>I am meeting our supplier tomorrow.</strong>'],
['be going to','am / is / are + going to + base verb','Intentions / predictions with present evidence<br><strong>We are going to redesign our logo.</strong>']])}
<h3>1. A timetable — Present Simple</h3>${ar('للحدث المقرر في جدول: يبدأ التدريب أو تفتح المنشأة في موعد. مع المفرد أضف s. في السؤال استخدم does ثم الفعل الأساسي.')}${example('The office opens at 8:30.<br>What time does the office open?')}
<h3>2. An arrangement — Present Continuous</h3>${ar('لترتيب مستقبلي اتفقت عليه أو جهزته: مقابلة عميل أو زيارة مورد. وجود الساعة لا يمنع استخدام هذا الزمن.')}${example('We are visiting the supplier at ten on Tuesday.<br>Are you meeting the new manager tomorrow?')}
<h3>3. An intention or prediction — be going to</h3>${ar('للنية: قرار تخطط لتنفيذه. وللتنبؤ: شيء تتوقعه بسبب دليل الآن. تأكد من وجود am/is/are ومن أن الفعل التالي بصيغته الأساسية.')}${example('We are going to recruit two assistants next month. (intention)<br>Look at those dark clouds. It is going to rain. (evidence)')}
${mistake('She meeting the client tomorrow.','She is meeting the client tomorrow.','Present Continuous يحتاج فعل be، وليس ing وحدها.')}
${mistake('The workshop start at nine.','The workshop starts at nine.','الفاعل مفرد؛ Present Simple يحتاج s هنا.')}
${mistake('They are going to opening a new office.','They are going to open a new office.','بعد going to نستخدم الفعل الأساسي.')}
<h3>Common exam trap</h3><p>A time expression alone does not decide the form. Context matters; more than one future form can be grammatical in an open sentence.</p>${ar('نختبر الصيغة أو المعنى المطلوب بوضوح؛ لا نزعم أن وجود موعد يجعل كل البدائل الأخرى خاطئة.')} `},
2:{title:'Connectors',what:'Words and phrases that show the relationship between ideas.',why:'Help your reader follow additions, contrasts, examples, time and sequence.',source:'Unit 2 Extra Activities p.2 + Key 2.2; Interactive Homework 2 p.2',body:()=>`
${ar('ابدأ بالعلاقة بين الفكرتين: إضافة؟ تعارض؟ مثال؟ ترتيب؟ ثم افحص التركيب وعلامات الترقيم. معنى الرابط وحده لا يكفي.')}
${table(['Function','Connectors','Position + original example'],[
['Adding ideas','and, also, as well as, in addition','The brand sells watches <strong>and</strong> bags.<br>It <strong>also</strong> sells shoes.<br><strong>In addition,</strong> it sells perfume.'],
['Contrasting ideas','but, however, although, while','The shop is small, <strong>but</strong> it is busy.<br>It is small. <strong>However,</strong> it is busy.'],
['Referring to time','previously, recently, when','<strong>Previously,</strong> we sold only watches.<br>Call me <strong>when</strong> you arrive.'],
['Giving examples','for example, for instance, such as','We sell accessories, <strong>such as</strong> belts and bags.'],
['Sequencing','first of all, to start with, then, finally','<strong>First of all,</strong> introduce the brand. <strong>Then,</strong> explain the campaign.']])}
<h3>Addition: choose the right structure</h3><p><strong>as well as + noun / -ing</strong>; <strong>in addition to + noun / -ing</strong>. Standalone <strong>In addition,</strong> introduces another idea.</p>${example('We sell bags as well as shoes.<br>In addition to selling bags, we sell shoes.<br>Our shop is small. It is also popular.')}${ar('also غالبًا قبل الفعل الأساسي وبعد be. ولا تتعامل مع as well as كأنها دائمًا بديل مباشر لـ and بين جملتين كاملتين.')}
<h3>Contrast: although vs however</h3>${example('Although the price is high, customers buy the product.<br>The price is high. However, customers buy the product.<br>The price is high; however, customers buy the product.')}${ar('although تبدأ جملة تابعة: although + فاعل + فعل. أما however فتربط فكرتين، ونستخدم هنا نقطة أو فاصلة منقوطة قبلها وفاصلة بعدها. لا نصل جملتين مستقلتين بفاصلة وحدها.')}
<p><strong>While</strong> can contrast two facts: “While one brand targets students, the other targets managers.” Read the context because while can also refer to time.</p>
<h3>Examples and order</h3>${example('We sell luxury products, such as watches.<br>Some brands use films. For example, a character may wear the company’s watch.<br>To start with, I’ll introduce the brand. Finally, I’ll answer questions.')}
${mistake('Although the logo is simple, but it is memorable.','Although the logo is simple, it is memorable.','لا نجمع although وbut بهذا الشكل في الجملة نفسها.')}
${mistake('In addition to we sell shoes.','In addition to bags, we sell shoes.','بعد in addition to استخدم اسمًا أو ing، وليس جملة مستقلة بهذا التركيب.')}
<h3>Common exam trap</h3><p>“For example” and “for instance” may both fit. A fair question must distinguish meaning or structure rather than reject an equally valid synonym.</p>`},
3:{title:'Indirect questions',what:'A question placed inside a polite opening.',why:'Ask about a job or clarify information with an appropriate opening.',source:'Unit 3 Extra Activities p.2 + Key 3.2; Interactive Workbook 3 p.2',body:()=>`
${ar('السؤال غير المباشر يبدأ بعبارة مثل Could you tell me…، ثم نرتب الجزء الداخلي كالجملة الخبرية: الفاعل قبل الفعل. هذا الدرس ليس Reported Speech.')}
${table(['Direct','Indirect','What changes?'],[
['What is your name?','Could you tell me <strong>what your name is</strong>?','your name + is → statement order'],
['Where does she work?','Do you know <strong>where she works</strong>?','Remove does; restore works'],
['When did he join?','Could you tell me <strong>when he joined</strong>?','Remove did; use joined'],
['Do you have experience?','Could you tell me <strong>if you have experience</strong>?','Yes/no → if / whether'],
['Is the role permanent?','I’d like to know <strong>whether the role is permanent</strong>.','Statement opening → full stop']])}
<h3>Step 1 · Keep the question word</h3><p>For <strong>what / where / when / why / how</strong>, keep that word. Put the subject before the verb.</p>${example('Where is the office?<br>Could you tell me where the office is?')}${ar('office هو الفاعل في الجزء الداخلي، لذلك يأتي قبل is. لا نكرر قلب ترتيب السؤال المباشر.')}
<h3>Step 2 · Remove question-only do / does / did</h3>${example('What does the job involve?<br>Could you tell me what the job involves?')}${ar('احذف does الخاصة بتكوين السؤال، ثم أعد s إلى الفعل لأن job مفرد. مع did يعود الفعل للماضي. لا تحذف do إذا كانت الفعل الأساسي بمعنى يفعل.')}
<h3>Step 3 · Yes/no needs if or whether</h3>${example('Do you offer training?<br>Could you tell me if you offer training?<br>Could you tell me whether you offer training?')}${ar('السؤال الذي إجابته نعم أو لا لا يحتوي أصلًا على wh-word؛ نستخدم if أو whether. لا نستبدل where أو when بهما لأن المعنى سيتغير.')}
<h3>Step 4 · Reverse the process</h3><p>“Could you tell me where she works?” becomes “Where does she work?” Restore <strong>does</strong> and the base verb <strong>work</strong>.</p>
${mistake('Could you tell me where is the office?','Could you tell me where the office is?','الترتيب الداخلي خبر: subject ثم verb.')}
${mistake('Do you know what does the role involve?','Do you know what the role involves?','لا تبقِ does داخل الجزء غير المباشر، وأعد s إلى involves.')}
<h3>Common exam trap</h3><p>Both if and whether can introduce a yes/no question here. We accept both in suitable free-text answers. Questions beginning “Could you…?” end with a question mark; “I’d like to know…” is a statement.</p>`}
};
const FUNCTIONS=[
{unit:1,title:'Greetings & introductions',purpose:'Start a first meeting and introduce people.',ar:'ابدأ اللقاء وعرّف بنفسك أو بزميلك.',phrase:'Good to finally meet you in person.',example:'Good to finally meet you in person, Lina. This is Omar, our sales manager.',mistake:'Use “This is Omar”, not “This Omar”.',source:'S28 p.3; S20 p.4'},
{unit:1,title:'Small talk',purpose:'Ask about the journey, location or work.',ar:'حديث قصير عن الرحلة أو مقر العمل لبدء التواصل.',phrase:'Did you have a good trip? / Where are you based?',example:'Where are you based? — I’m based in Jeddah.',mistake:'“Where are you based?” asks about work location, not job title.',source:'S28 pp.3–4; S20 p.4'},
{unit:1,title:'Offering hospitality',purpose:'Make a visitor comfortable.',ar:'اعرض ضيافة مناسبة؛ هذه مجموعة الضيافة في U1.',phrase:'Can I get you something to drink?',example:'Can I get you something to drink? — Water would be lovely, thank you.',mistake:'A drink offer needs an acceptance or polite refusal, not a job description.',source:'S20 p.4'},
{unit:1,title:'Saying goodbye',purpose:'Close a meeting politely.',ar:'اختم اللقاء بتمنّي رحلة موفقة أو توديع مناسب.',phrase:'Have a good trip home.',example:'It was good to meet you. Have a good trip home.',mistake:'Use a closing phrase at the end, not as your first introduction.',source:'S28 p.3; S20 p.4'},
{unit:2,title:'Giving advice',purpose:'Suggest a practical action.',ar:'اقترح إجراءً يساعد زميلك، وانتبه لصيغة الفعل.',phrase:'Why don’t you + base verb? / Have you tried + -ing?',example:'Why don’t you ask the team? Have you tried changing the meeting time?',mistake:'Have you tried asking…? Not: Have you tried ask…?',source:'S29 p.3; S21 p.4'},
{unit:2,title:'Responding to advice',purpose:'Accept advice or say you will consider it.',ar:'يمكن قبول النصيحة أو التفكير فيها دون وعد بالتنفيذ.',phrase:'That’s a good idea. / OK, I’ll think about it.',example:'That’s a good idea. I’ll ask my manager this afternoon.',mistake:'“I’ll think about it” does not promise that you will do it.',source:'S46 p.9, original activity 9A screenshot'},
{unit:2,title:'Presentation signposting',purpose:'Guide listeners through the opening, sections and closing.',ar:'بيّن هدف العرض، ثم انتقالاتك، ثم الختام والأسئلة.',phrase:'Let me begin with… / Finally… / Thank you for listening.',example:'Today I want to introduce our brand. Let me begin with our logo. Finally, I’ll explain our campaign.',mistake:'“Firstly” opens a sequence; “Finally” introduces its last part.',source:'S29 p.4; S21 p.4; Course Pack p.7'},
{unit:3,title:'Job interviews',purpose:'Ask about the role and next steps.',ar:'اسأل عن الدور الوظيفي والخطوة التالية في المقابلة.',phrase:'Could you tell me more about…? / What are the next steps?',example:'Could you tell me more about the training? What are the next steps?',mistake:'Could you tell me what the next steps are? Not: …what are the next steps?',source:'S30 p.4; S24 p.4'},
{unit:3,title:'Active listening & summarising',purpose:'Restate the key idea to check your interpretation.',ar:'أعد الفكرة بأسلوبك لتتأكد من فهمها.',phrase:'So, it’s important for you…',example:'So, it’s important for you to finish the report before Thursday.',mistake:'Summarising checks the speaker’s meaning; it does not automatically show agreement.',source:'S30 p.3; S24 p.4'},
{unit:3,title:'Clarifying',purpose:'Ask the speaker to explain a term or idea.',ar:'اطلب تفسير كلمة أو فكرة بدل افتراض المقصود.',phrase:'What do you mean by…?',example:'What do you mean by “flexible hours”?',mistake:'A clarification question asks for meaning, not a change of subject.',source:'S30 p.3; S24 p.4'},
{unit:3,title:'Checking & correcting understanding',purpose:'Identify uncertainty or correct a misunderstanding.',ar:'صرّح بالغموض أو صحح ما فُهم خطأ.',phrase:'I’m not clear about… / No, that’s not what I said.',example:'I’m not clear about the deadline. — The report is due on Wednesday.',mistake:'Clarify the specific unclear point instead of guessing.',source:'S30 p.3; S24 p.4'},
{unit:3,title:'Giving listening feedback',purpose:'Show that you have heard and understood the concern.',ar:'أظهر أنك تتفاعل مع ما يقوله الطرف الآخر.',phrase:'OK, that’s very useful to know. / I can see you are concerned.',example:'I can see you are concerned about the interview. Tell me more.',mistake:'Listening feedback here is not the separate Unit 8 performance-feedback lesson.',source:'S30 p.3; S24 p.4'}
];
const READINGS={
1:{title:'Inside Northline',text:'Northline is a small business that makes office furniture. Production makes the desks, while Quality Control checks every batch. The sales team works closely with Marketing, but it reports to the sales director. Customer Service looks after questions from buyers. Next Tuesday, Sara is meeting a new supplier; they agreed on the visit yesterday. According to the timetable, the factory tour starts at 9:30. Northline is also going to recruit two assistants because its current team needs support.',source:'Original reading; skills grounded in S20 p.3, S28 pp.1–2,5'},
2:{title:'A new direction for Mera',text:'Mera sells leather bags. Its logo is simple, and many customers recognise it. However, the company wants people to associate the brand with reliable service, not only with its design. It is asking customers to share ideas online and responding to their comments. Next year, Mera plans to sell travel accessories under the same brand name. It is taking a cautious approach: first, it will test a small collection in one store. Finally, it will review customer feedback before expanding further afield.',source:'Original reading; skills grounded in S29 pp.1–2,5; S21 p.1'},
3:{title:'Preparing for an interview',text:'Rana is applying for a customer service internship. She has updated her CV and included a short example of how she solved a problem in a student project. Before the interview, she reads about the employer and practises explaining her experience. She avoids calling herself “the perfect candidate” without evidence. During the interview, she listens carefully and asks for clarification when a question is unclear. At the end, she asks about training and the next steps. She wants to gain experience and show how her skills can be of value to the company.',source:'Original reading; skills grounded in S24 p.3; S30 pp.1,4–5'}
};
const LESSONS=[];
for(let unit=1;unit<=3;unit++){
const meta=[['vocab','Words that do the work','Vocabulary & collocations','Vocabulary'],['grammar',GRAMMAR[unit].title,'Understand the form. Practise the choice.','Grammar'],['functional',['','First meetings','Advice & presentations','Interviews & active listening'][unit],'Choose the phrase for the situation.','Functional Language'],['reading','Read, understand, respond','Original reading & practical writing','Reading'],['pronunciation',['','Plural endings','/ɪz/ & useful pauses','a / an & sentence stress'][unit],'Written guidance; no audio recording','Pronunciation']];
meta.forEach(([type,title,subtitle,category],i)=>LESSONS.push({id:`${unit}-${type}`,unit,type,title,subtitle,category,number:i+1}));
}
const BANK=[];
function add(unit,category,prompt,choices,answer,explanation,extra={}){BANK.push({id:'q'+(BANK.length+1),unit,category,prompt,choices,answer,explanation,source:category==='Grammar'?GRAMMAR[unit].source:`Unit ${unit} content map; ${['','S28 / S20','S29 / S21','S30 / S24'][unit]}`,type:choices?'mcq':'text',...extra});}
// Original questions. Sources identify the skill, never a reproduced exam question.
add(1,'Grammar','Use Present Simple for the published timetable: The seminar ___ at 10.',['starts','is start','starting','start'],'starts','A singular subject takes -s in Present Simple. الجدول المعلن: starts مع المفرد.');
add(1,'Grammar','Complete the Present Continuous arrangement: We ___ visiting the supplier tomorrow.',['are','is','be','do'],'are','Present Continuous = am/is/are + -ing. مع we نستخدم are.');
add(1,'Grammar','Use be going to: Our team is going to ___ a new assistant.',['hire','hiring','hired','hires'],'hire','After going to, use the base verb. بعد going to الفعل الأساسي.');
add(1,'Grammar','Which sentence is a correctly formed future arrangement?',['I am meeting the buyer on Monday.','I meeting the buyer on Monday.','I am meet the buyer on Monday.','I am meets the buyer on Monday.'],'I am meeting the buyer on Monday.','am + meeting forms the continuous. يجب وجود be وing معًا.');
add(1,'Grammar','The train ___ at 7:15 according to the timetable. Use Present Simple.',['leaves','leave','leaving','is leave'],'leaves','The train is singular; the requested timetable form is leaves.');
add(1,'Grammar','Complete the question: What time does the workshop ___?',['begin','begins','beginning','began'],'begin','After does, use the base form. لا نضيف s بعد does.');
add(1,'Grammar','Use the base verb after going to: They are going to ___ (open) another branch.',null,'open','going to + base verb: open، وليس opening.');
add(1,'Grammar','Fill the missing auxiliary: I ___ meeting the director this afternoon.',null,'am','I + am + -ing. هذا ترتيب مستقبلي.');
add(1,'Grammar','“We agreed yesterday: I am visiting their office tomorrow.” What does the future form express?',['An arrangement','A published timetable','A past habit','An instruction'],'An arrangement','The speakers already agreed on the visit. اتفاق سابق يوضح معنى الترتيب.');
add(1,'Grammar','Match each form to the use shown.',null,{a:'Published timetable',b:'Future arrangement',c:'Intention'},'Match by meaning, not by the presence of a time. اربط الزمن بالسياق.',{type:'match',pairs:[['a','The tour starts at nine (official schedule).'],['b','I am meeting Sara tomorrow (we agreed).'],['c','We are going to redesign our logo (our intention).']],matchOptions:['Intention','Published timetable','Future arrangement']});
add(2,'Grammar','We sell watches ___ jewellery. Choose the addition connector.',['and','although','however','when'],'and','And adds one item to another. and للإضافة.');
add(2,'Grammar','___ the shop is small, it attracts many customers.',['Although','However','In addition','Such as'],'Although','Although + subject + verb introduces contrast. تأتي بعدها جملة كاملة.');
add(2,'Grammar','The product is expensive. ___, demand is strong. Choose contrast.',['However','In addition','For example','Finally'],'However','However contrasts two ideas and is followed by a comma here.');
add(2,'Grammar','We sell accessories, ___ belts and wallets.',['such as','although','however','when'],'such as','Such as introduces examples within this sentence. هنا تأتي بعدها أسماء.');
add(2,'Grammar','Choose the correctly punctuated contrast.',['Sales rose. However, costs also rose.','Sales rose however costs also rose.','Sales rose, however costs also rose.','Sales rose. However costs also rose.'],'Sales rose. However, costs also rose.','Use a full stop before However and a comma after it in this pattern.');
add(2,'Grammar','Complete the expression: In addition ___ bags, we sell shoes.',null,'to','In addition to + noun. احفظ التركيب مع to.');
add(2,'Grammar','Complete the expression: We sell bags as ___ as shoes.',null,'well','As well as adds an item. لا تنسَ well بين as وas.');
add(2,'Grammar','Choose the correct sentence.',['Although the brand is new, it is popular.','Although the brand is new, but it is popular.','Although the brand new, it popular.','Although is new, the brand popular.'],'Although the brand is new, it is popular.','Although already marks contrast; do not add but in this structure.');
add(2,'Grammar','Which word refers to an earlier time?',['Previously','Finally','However','Also'],'Previously','Previously means before now / before that time. سابقًا.');
add(2,'Grammar','Match the connector to its function.',null,{a:'Giving examples',b:'Contrasting ideas',c:'Adding ideas'},'For example illustrates; however contrasts; also adds.',{type:'match',pairs:[['a','for example'],['b','however'],['c','also']],matchOptions:['Adding ideas','Giving examples','Contrasting ideas']});
add(3,'Grammar','Choose the correct indirect question.',['Could you tell me where the office is?','Could you tell me where is the office?','Could you tell me where does the office is?','Could you tell me where the office be?'],'Could you tell me where the office is?','Inside the question, use subject + verb: the office is.');
add(3,'Grammar','Do you know what the role ___?',['involves','does involves','involve does','is involve'],'involves','Remove does from the embedded question; role is singular, so involves.');
add(3,'Grammar','“Do you offer training?” needs which connector in an indirect question?',['if or whether','where','when','whose'],'if or whether','This is yes/no, so if or whether is suitable. كلاهما مقبول هنا.');
add(3,'Grammar','Complete: Could you tell me ___ you have a driving licence? Use a yes/no connector.',null,['if','whether'],'Both if and whether introduce the yes/no question.');
add(3,'Grammar','Rewrite “Where is the interview?” Start with “Could you tell me”.',null,'Could you tell me where the interview is?','Keep where; put the interview before is. ترتيب خبري داخل السؤال.');
add(3,'Grammar','Turn into a direct question: “Could you tell me where she works?”',null,'Where does she work?','Restore does for the direct question; works becomes work.');
add(3,'Grammar','Choose the direct version of “Do you know when the course starts?”',['When does the course start?','When the course starts?','When does the course starts?','When is the course start?'],'When does the course start?','A direct Present Simple question uses does + base verb.');
add(3,'Grammar','Complete: Do you know when he ___ the company? (join, past simple)',null,'joined','The embedded clause is a statement: he joined. Do not keep did here.');
add(3,'Grammar','Choose a correctly formed statement.',['I’d like to know whether the role is permanent.','I’d like to know whether is the role permanent.','I’d like to know does the role permanent.','I’d like to know whether the role permanent.'],'I’d like to know whether the role is permanent.','Statement order follows whether; I’d like to know ends as a statement.');
add(3,'Grammar','Direct → indirect: “What is your name?” Complete: Could you tell me ___?',null,'what your name is','Wh-word + subject + verb. ما اسمك؟ تصبح what your name is داخل السؤال.');
add(1,'Functional Language','You meet a new supplier for the first time. Choose the introduction.',['Good to finally meet you in person.','Have a good trip home.','Finally, I’ll take questions.','I’m responsible for billing.'],'Good to finally meet you in person.','This welcomes someone at a first meeting. عبارة للتعارف أول مرة.');
add(1,'Functional Language','A visitor arrives after a flight. Ask about the journey.',['Did you have a good trip?','What are the next steps?','Could you explain the logo?','When does production begin?'],'Did you have a good trip?','A journey question is appropriate small talk. سؤال عن الرحلة.');
add(1,'Functional Language','“Can I get you something to drink?” Choose the relevant reply.',['Tea would be lovely, thank you.','I report to the director.','The meeting is in Room 2.','It begins next week.'],'Tea would be lovely, thank you.','Accept the offer by naming a drink and thanking the host.');
add(1,'Functional Language','“Where are you based?” Which answer fits?',['At our Jeddah office.','I joined in April.','I manage four people.','The trip was comfortable.'],'At our Jeddah office.','Based asks about location. السؤال عن مكان العمل.');
add(1,'Functional Language','Match the phrase to the situation.',null,{a:'Introduction',b:'Hospitality',c:'Goodbye'},'Each phrase has a different conversational purpose.',{type:'match',pairs:[['a','This is our new colleague, Sami.'],['b','Can I take your coat?'],['c','Have a good trip home.']],matchOptions:['Goodbye','Introduction','Hospitality']});
add(2,'Functional Language','Complete the advice: Have you tried ___ the team?',['asking','ask','asked','to asking'],'asking','Have you tried + -ing suggests an action to try.');
add(2,'Functional Language','Complete: Why don’t you ___ your manager?',['call','calling','called','to call'],'call','Why don’t you + base verb. لا نضيف to أو ing.');
add(2,'Functional Language','A colleague suggests an idea. Which reply says you will consider it, without committing?',['OK, I’ll think about it.','I’ll definitely do it now.','I already finished it.','Today I’ll present our results.'],'OK, I’ll think about it.','Considering an idea is different from promising to act.');
add(2,'Functional Language','Which phrase introduces the final section of a presentation?',['Finally, I’ll explain our plan.','Firstly, I’ll introduce myself.','Thank you for the advice.','What do you mean by that?'],'Finally, I’ll explain our plan.','Finally marks the last section.');
add(2,'Functional Language','Match the presentation phrase to its purpose.',null,{a:'State the objective',b:'Begin the first section',c:'Close the presentation'},'Signposts help listeners follow the structure.',{type:'match',pairs:[['a','Today I want to explain our campaign.'],['b','Let me begin with our customers.'],['c','Thank you for listening.']],matchOptions:['Close the presentation','State the objective','Begin the first section']});
add(3,'Functional Language','You do not understand “flexible hours”. Choose a clarification.',['What do you mean by flexible hours?','Thank you for your time.','I agree to start tomorrow.','Have a safe journey.'],'What do you mean by flexible hours?','Clarifying asks for the meaning of an unclear expression.');
